# React Native rules (JS/TS layer, Expo config); native trees use the native rule sets
# Generated from the threat library cards (threats/android, threats/ios, threats/shared); each rule cites its card.
# Fields (tab-separated, "-" = empty):
#   rule_id threat_id severity type file_globs pattern message card flags [exclude]
# Severity: high/critical block the build by default; medium/low warn.
# Heuristic rules are kept one level below the card severity so they warn.
RN-ST-001	sensitive-data-in-client-storage	medium	imatch	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	(asyncstorage\.(setitem|multiset)|mmkv[a-z]*\.set|storage\.set)\([[:space:]]*["'`][^"'`]*(token|password|passwd|secret|jwt|session|cvv)	Heuristic: credential stored in AsyncStorage/MMKV (unencrypted): use react-native-keychain or expo-secure-store	shared/data-privacy/sensitive-data-in-client-storage.md	-	SecureStore|Keychain|EncryptedStorage
RN-WV-001	android-webview-file-access	high	match	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	(allowFileAccess|allowFileAccessFromFileURLs|allowUniversalAccessFromFileURLs)([[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*\{[[:space:]]*true|[[:space:]]*/?>|[[:space:]]*$|[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*true)	WebView file access is enabled: remove allowFileAccess* props (default false) and bundle pages as assets	android/webview/android-webview-file-access.md	-
RN-WV-002	android-webview-tls-bypass	high	match	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	mixedContentMode[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*\{?[[:space:]]*["']always	Mixed content allowed in the WebView: use mixedContentMode="never"	android/webview/android-webview-tls-bypass.md	-
RN-WV-003	android-webview-untrusted-content	medium	match	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	originWhitelist[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*\{[[:space:]]*\[[[:space:]]*["']\*["']	originWhitelist ["*"] lets the WebView open any scheme/origin: list your exact https origins	android/webview/android-webview-untrusted-content.md	-
RN-WV-004	ios-wkwebview-message-handlers	high	match	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	injectJavaScript\([[:space:]]*`[^`]*\$\{|injectedJavaScript(BeforeContentLoaded)?[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*\{[[:space:]]*`[^`]*\$\{	Injected JavaScript is built by string interpolation (script injection): JSON.stringify the data and post it with postMessage	ios/webview/ios-wkwebview-message-handlers.md	-
RN-WV-005	android-webview-javascript-interface	medium	check	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	cooccur;;onMessage[[:space:]]*=;;<WebView;;!nativeEvent\.(url|origin)	Heuristic: WebView onMessage handler does not check where the message came from: verify event.nativeEvent.url/origin before acting	android/webview/android-webview-javascript-interface.md	-
RN-TLS-001	incorrect-certificate-validation	critical	match	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	rejectUnauthorized[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*false|NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED[^;]*["']?0|disableAllSecurity[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*true|trustAllCerts|ignoreSslErrors?[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*\{?[[:space:]]*true	TLS certificate validation is disabled: remove the override	shared/crypto/incorrect-certificate-validation.md	-
RN-LOG-001	sensitive-data-in-logs	high	match	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	console\.(log|info|warn|error|debug)\(.*(\$\{|\+[[:space:]]*|,[[:space:]]*)[A-Za-z_.]*([Pp]assword|[Pp]asswd|[Tt]oken|[Ss]ecret|[Jj]wt|JWT|[Cc]vv|CVV|[Oo]tp[^a-z]|OTP|PASSWORD|TOKEN|SECRET)	Credential written to the device log: remove it or log a redacted value (strip console.* in release with babel-plugin-transform-remove-console)	shared/data-privacy/sensitive-data-in-logs.md	-
RN-DL-001	ios-deep-link-abuse	low	check	*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx	cooccur;;Linking\.(getInitialURL|addEventListener)|useURL\(;;!new[[:space:]]+URL\(|URLSearchParams|[Aa]llowed|ALLOWED_|startsWith\(|Linking\.parse|parse\(	Heuristic: deep-link handler shows no URL validation: parse the URL and allow-list host/path/params before acting	ios/webview/ios-deep-link-abuse.md	-
RN-SEC-001	secrets-leakage	high	match	.env;.env.*;*.env;*.js;*.jsx;*.ts;*.tsx;app.json;app.config.*	EXPO_PUBLIC_[A-Z0-9_]*(SECRET|PRIVATE|PASSWORD)	EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the app bundle: never put secrets in public env variables	shared/data-privacy/secrets-leakage.md	skippath=\.(example|sample|template)$
RN-EXPO-001	attacker-in-the-middle	high	match	app.json;app.config.*	["']?usesCleartextTraffic["']?[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*true|["']?NSAllowsArbitraryLoads["']?[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*true	Expo config allows cleartext HTTP: remove usesCleartextTraffic / NSAllowsArbitraryLoads	shared/network/attacker-in-the-middle.md	-
RN-EXPO-002	android-backup-exposure	medium	match	app.json;app.config.*	["']?allowBackup["']?[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*true	Expo config enables Android backups: set android.allowBackup to false	android/storage/android-backup-exposure.md	-
RN-HERM-001	android-reverse-engineering	high	match	*.gradle;*.gradle.kts;gradle.properties;app.json;app.config.*	hermesEnabled[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*false|enableHermes[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*false|["']?jsEngine["']?[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*["']jsc["']	Hermes is off, so the JS bundle ships as readable source: keep Hermes on (bytecode) and run R8 on the Android host	android/integrity/android-reverse-engineering.md	-
